# SRG-APP-000855-WSR-000240  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, require immediate
# selection of a new password upon account recovery.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000855-WSR-000240
group:           V-264350
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004063
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None: Splunk Web presents the login and password-change pages but exposes
                 no self-service recovery flow and no setting that forces a new password
                 after a reset; web.conf [settings] carries only the login page hint text,
                 and authentication.conf has no change-at-next-login key.

external:        The recovery procedure and the obligation to change the password
                 immediately after it - carried by the organization's account-management
                 procedure.
external:        Where authentication is external (LDAP, SAML, ProxySSO) or fronted by an
                 SSO proxy, the recovery flow and any forced change belong to that
                 provider.

manual_reason:   No conf key represents account recovery or a forced change at next login
                 for the web tier, so no observed configuration value can decide this
                 requirement.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:509;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:1430 (loginPasswordHint - login page text
                 only, no recovery flow)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Web has no setting that
                 requires selection of a new password upon account recovery, so this
                 requirement is carried by the organization's account-management procedure
                 and by the identity provider where authentication is external; this
                 determination is from the perspective of the application layer alone.
